# V90Phase4Demodulator: the V.90 / V.92 phase-4 (RX) state machine (the demodulator side of phase 4: Ri / RiNot, TRN2d known data with the linear mapping study, MP / CP / Ed, B1d, the RRN silence echo
# energy measurement, Rt / RtNot / Rf), 0x351c bytes on i386, a plain class (no vptr, no base class); V90Demodulator embeds it.  It EMBEDS a V90Phase4Modulator (+0x50, the P30 class, 0x2fac B: the signal it knows,
# flattened here as mod_*) and TWO V90RDetector objects (+0x2ffc r_ for R / Rt / Ri / RiNot, +0x3028 rf_ for Rf / Rd detection; the P06 class, 0x2c B each).  The objects it USES (V90Demapper, V90Descrambler<uchar,int>,
# V90MP, V90CP, V90ConnectionEvaluator, V90MappingParams x2, V90Parameters, V90AutoDigitalImpDetector, V90Phase3Demodulator) are plain pointers (the C1 constructor's arguments).  Member names are descriptive.
# The V90Demapper member at +0x1eb4 (p28 `z1eb4_`, "zeroed by reset, never read" there) IS read here: it is the flag "linear mapping study enabled" (written 1 / 0 by getV90 / getV92Decision state 3).
